PtokaX 0.5.3.2 - Hotel fork
---------------------------

Very early on trying to change things up. Probably should use a different versioning
approach. Main changes are discoverable via the ptokaxctl interface. Just check the
ADMIN-GUIDE. I've tried to keep it short and sensible.

This is PtokaX version without gui able to run from console or as windows service.
You can use for that version config files from gui version of PtokaX or you can create own config files, see examples in cfg.example directory.

Command line commands available:
-c <configdir>		- absolute path to PtokaX config directory (where will PtokaX have cfg, logs, scripts and texts directories).
-h					- show help.
-m					- show PtokaX configuration menu.
-v					- show PtokaX version with build date and time.
/generatexmllanguage	- generate english language example file.

PtokaX runs in the foreground; use a service manager to run it as a service. See
contrib/systemd/README.systemd, which also covers binding ports below 1024.

When no config dir is specified the current directory is used.

If it does not start, check the journal, or the logs directory when not running under
a service manager.

Signals:
SIGHUP				- restart the scripts.
SIGUSR1				- reopen the files in the logs directory, for use after a rotation.

Homepage: http://www.PtokaX.org

PtokaX Forum: http://forum.PtokaX.org

PtokaX Wiki: http://wiki.PtokaX.org

Please report all bugs on forum or to PPK@PtokaX.org or to me (PPK) on 'PtokaX Dev Hub' dchub://PXdev.CzDC.org:2002

Note: This version have Lua scripting interface incompatible with all scripts for 0.3.6.0c and older !
Note: IP to Country database files will need to be acquired separately. I used this repo to create mine: https://github.com/emulefanscom/ip-to-country-csv-converter (you may need to modify the behavior to get IPv6 output). Mind the IPV4 vs IPV6 differences. Unpack them to PtokaX/cfg directory.

Latest PtokaX changelog: http://wiki.PtokaX.org/doku.php?id=changelog
